{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_d6f4ccc1f4c6c5ec12b2f4e768adbc0ad5db5e2f467af196765302958df5078e", "title": "Dimebag Darrell", "text": "Darrell Abbott (August 20, 1966 – December 8, 2004), also known as Diamond Darrell and Dimebag Darrell, was an American musician and songwriter who was a co-founder of Pantera alongside his brother Vinnie Paul, and founder of Damageplan. He was considered to be one of the driving forces behind groove metal.", "score": 23.911}, {"id": "hp_doc_0a082d5528e7b07960a4aef66d672d1fa57efdbda18ba9e5f0d7448749cb5aea", "title": "Songs for the Incurable Heart", "text": "Songs for the Incurable Heart is STEMM's second full-length album originally released November 15, 2005. It was re-released on October 10, 2006 by major record label I Scream Records, who signed STEMM in 2006. The song \"The Day the Earth Stood Still\" is a tribute song to the victims of the September 11, 2001 attacks in which vocalist T.J. Frost was a survivor. The opening track, \"The Memory Remains\" is also a tribute song to former Pantera/Damageplan guitarist Darrell \"Dimebag\" Abbott. This album is the last to feature former vocalist T.J. Frost and guitarist Rich Spalla who both left the band in 2007. The album sold over 6,000 copies.", "score": 11.5385}, {"id": "hp_doc_84fb004c54760d505f5b1d7fa4f9b55ada8ef51894f44489be2e87af4df4a9f9", "title": "Twin Dragons", "text": "Twin Dragons (also known as Shuang long hui and Brother vs. Brother) is a 1992 Hong Kong action comedy film directed by Ringo Lam and Tsui Hark, and starring Jackie Chan in two roles as a pair of twin brothers.", "score": 6.9286}], "remaining_searches": 1}
